    family: 'Not an alphabet: early modern Icelandic sign-magic. Each stave is a single drawn figure, usually named, with a stated purpose, written in the manuscript books of magic (galdrakver, galdraskræður) from about 1500 to the nineteenth century. The staves have no sound values; some contain runes or rune-like strokes. They belong with the charaktêres and the Solomonic seals, not with the runic alphabets.',
    keyedTo: 'none',
